<Placemark>
	<name>Samaga old village site 2026-11-06 10:19:33</name>
	<description><![CDATA[<!-- desc_gen:start -->
<font color="black"><table width="100%"><tr><td width="100%" align="center"><a href="files/1000060791.jpg" target="_blank"><img src="files/1000060791.jpg" width="60px" align="right" style="border: 3px white solid;"></a><br /><br /><a href="files/1000060790.jpg" target="_blank"><img src="files/1000060790.jpg" width="60px" align="right" style="border: 3px white solid;"></a><br /><br />
<!-- desc_user:start -->
A village that no longer exists. Only a few coconut trees remain where it once stood. According to a local villager in Biriri, in 1991 the clan living here relocated to Biriri village to settle with the rest of the community, so they could be close to the church established there.
<!-- desc_user:end -->
